1
00:00:22,581 --> 00:00:25,041
Hey! Are you okay?

2
00:00:26,081 --> 00:00:27,211
Who's that?

3
00:00:28,501 --> 00:00:29,671
He's big.

4
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:33,341
What about the duel?

5
00:00:35,931 --> 00:00:38,681
What did he say? Duel?

6
00:00:42,021 --> 00:00:45,351
Duel? This isn't the time to be sleeping!

7
00:00:45,441 --> 00:00:46,771
He got up!

8
00:00:46,851 --> 00:00:48,901
He's still alive!

9
00:00:48,981 --> 00:00:50,321
Looks like you can still fight.

10
00:00:50,401 --> 00:00:51,231
UNITED FRONT

11
00:00:51,321 --> 00:00:52,781
I'll give you a minute to recover.

12
00:00:52,861 --> 00:00:55,201
Don't underestimate me! Come on! Attack me!

13
00:00:55,281 --> 00:00:58,411
No. I can't fight you when you're like that.

14
00:00:58,491 --> 00:01:01,161
Shut up! I don't need your sympathy!

15
00:01:04,461 --> 00:01:06,621
I was right. See?

16
00:01:06,711 --> 00:01:09,421
Hey! Old man! Stop!

17
00:01:09,501 --> 00:01:12,671
Let him do it. Someone, bring a chair.

18
00:01:16,221 --> 00:01:17,181
Let me see.

19
00:01:17,261 --> 00:01:20,851
Stay away, baldy! Go treat your own wounds.

20
00:01:20,931 --> 00:01:21,891
Just let me see.

21
00:01:21,971 --> 00:01:23,311
Don't touch me!

22
00:01:24,391 --> 00:01:28,481
Don't get so mad. It's a bad habit of yours.
Use your head.

23
00:01:30,111 --> 00:01:33,781
What do you think you should do right now to win?

24
00:01:35,361 --> 00:01:38,821
I haven't had that much fun in a long time, Thorfinn.

25
00:01:38,911 --> 00:01:41,661
I'll tell you, just like I promised.

26
00:01:42,911 --> 00:01:43,991
About your father,

27
00:01:44,951 --> 00:01:46,751
Thors.

28
00:03:19,471 --> 00:03:22,181
You know who the Jomsvikings are, right?

29
00:03:22,261 --> 00:03:26,011
Thors and I were both commanders.

30
00:03:27,061 --> 00:03:30,351
Thors was particularly strong.

31
00:03:31,601 --> 00:03:35,901
The Jomsvikings don't accept average warriors.

32
00:03:35,981 --> 00:03:38,361
Thors was so good that they nicknamed him
"The Troll."

33
00:03:39,361 --> 00:03:44,241
Their leader, Sigvaldi, liked him and gave him
one of his daughters.

34
00:03:44,321 --> 00:03:47,951
She's your mother, Helga.

35
00:03:48,621 --> 00:03:52,291
The leader of the Jomsvikings is my grandfather?

36
00:03:52,371 --> 00:03:56,251
That's right. He's also my older brother.

37
00:03:56,341 --> 00:04:00,301
In other words, that means I'm your great-uncle.

38
00:04:01,671 --> 00:04:03,971
He's related to the captain? No way!

39
00:04:05,261 --> 00:04:10,471
Our last battle was the Battle of Hjörungavágr in Norway.
We lost that battle.

40
00:04:11,981 --> 00:04:16,231
During the naval battle, Thors fell into the sea
and didn't come back up.

41
00:04:17,691 --> 00:04:19,941
I cried.

42
00:04:20,031 --> 00:04:24,611
I wanted to beat him someday. With my own hands.

43
00:04:26,071 --> 00:04:29,121
But Thors wasn't dead.

44
00:04:30,161 --> 00:04:31,871
The last time I saw him was in Jomsborg.

45
00:04:31,951 --> 00:04:33,211
987 BC
JOMSBORG HOME BASE OF JOMSVIKINGS

46
00:04:33,291 --> 00:04:35,041
It was three months after his funeral.

47
00:04:36,461 --> 00:04:38,791
Then he got scared and peed his pants.

48
00:04:38,881 --> 00:04:40,091
Seriously?

49
00:04:40,171 --> 00:04:42,261
The patrol just left. Let's go.

50
00:04:47,931 --> 00:04:49,471
Hey!

51
00:04:51,141 --> 00:04:53,231
Are you guys thieves?

52
00:04:54,771 --> 00:04:59,151
Did you know this house belongs to Thors,
a leader in the Jomsvikings?

53
00:04:59,231 --> 00:05:01,231
Thorkell.

54
00:05:01,321 --> 00:05:04,151
I usually leave thieves alone, but...

55
00:05:09,781 --> 00:05:13,201
I just lost one of my friends.

56
00:05:13,291 --> 00:05:15,251
I've been in a bad mood these days.

57
00:05:23,631 --> 00:05:27,091
Thors? You-- What?

58
00:05:27,181 --> 00:05:30,721
Come on! Where have you been?

59
00:05:30,801 --> 00:05:34,101
We held your funeral!

60
00:05:34,181 --> 00:05:37,021
Okay, okay. Calm down, Thorkell!

61
00:05:37,101 --> 00:05:40,111
Sorry for making you worry.

62
00:05:40,191 --> 00:05:41,771
It's Helga!

63
00:05:41,861 --> 00:05:45,151
What's wrong? You guys are both dressed
in shabby clothes!

64
00:05:45,241 --> 00:05:46,741
Excuse me, Uncle Thorkell--

65
00:05:46,821 --> 00:05:50,371
I knew it! You'd never die over something
as little as falling into the sea!

66
00:05:50,451 --> 00:05:52,331
Excuse me, Uncle. We--

67
00:05:52,411 --> 00:05:57,251
Have you seen my brother yet? No?
All right! I'll go wake him up for you.

68
00:05:57,331 --> 00:05:58,621
Thorkell.

69
00:05:58,711 --> 00:05:59,921
Listen to me.

70
00:06:00,001 --> 00:06:03,251
Okay! Let's catch up inside.

71
00:06:06,551 --> 00:06:07,381
What's wrong?

72
00:06:10,801 --> 00:06:13,061
I'm not going to see the leader.

73
00:06:13,141 --> 00:06:15,061
We're leaving here.

74
00:06:15,141 --> 00:06:19,601
To do what? You can leave tomorrow!
You just came back.

75
00:06:20,771 --> 00:06:21,771
I'm leaving...

76
00:06:23,021 --> 00:06:25,031
this town and the Jomsvikings.

77
00:06:26,281 --> 00:06:29,491
Please forget that you saw me tonight.

78
00:06:33,491 --> 00:06:35,661
What? Is this a joke?

79
00:06:35,741 --> 00:06:38,001
Just pretend that I'm dead.

80
00:06:39,041 --> 00:06:40,581
Please, Thorkell.

81
00:06:42,751 --> 00:06:46,341
I don't understand. What are you talking about?

82
00:06:48,971 --> 00:06:50,431
I've decided.

83
00:06:54,681 --> 00:06:57,021
I'm not going to fight anymore.

84
00:06:58,061 --> 00:07:01,351
I said I don't understand!

85
00:07:01,441 --> 00:07:04,271
You're not scared because you almost died, right?

86
00:07:04,361 --> 00:07:08,191
My brother is considering you as his successor.

87
00:07:08,281 --> 00:07:09,401
Sorry.

88
00:07:11,281 --> 00:07:15,121
You're tired, right? Just eat something
and go to sleep for today.

89
00:07:17,371 --> 00:07:20,121
Now I understand.

90
00:07:22,461 --> 00:07:24,631
I understand what a real warrior is.

91
00:07:27,051 --> 00:07:30,131
So, I can't stay here anymore.

92
00:07:41,481 --> 00:07:46,521
You know the rules, right? Anyone who leaves without
the leader's permission will be sentenced to death.

93
00:07:49,531 --> 00:07:51,951
This is the capital of warriors.

94
00:07:52,031 --> 00:07:55,661
You don't know how to do anything except fight.
Where are you going?

95
00:07:56,581 --> 00:07:59,241
Somewhere, but not here.

96
00:08:03,291 --> 00:08:04,251
Thors.

97
00:08:04,331 --> 00:08:06,671
It'll be okay. Stay back.

98
00:08:11,341 --> 00:08:13,131
Take care, Thorkell.

99
00:08:14,131 --> 00:08:15,721
Where's your sword?

100
00:08:16,721 --> 00:08:17,551
I don't need it.

101
00:08:28,571 --> 00:08:32,401
When I woke up, Thors was already gone.

102
00:08:33,991 --> 00:08:39,201
Fifteen years later, I found out that
Thors had really died.

103
00:08:40,451 --> 00:08:43,411
I thought about him for 15 years.

104
00:08:43,501 --> 00:08:47,001
I realized that whether the body is still alive
or not doesn't matter.

105
00:08:48,091 --> 00:08:52,171
What's important for a warrior is where their soul is.

106
00:08:53,551 --> 00:08:55,931
His soul had gone somewhere far away.

107
00:08:56,971 --> 00:08:59,261
I don't understand it yet.

108
00:08:59,351 --> 00:09:01,851
Somewhere I can't reach yet.

109
00:09:01,931 --> 00:09:03,981
Somewhere, but not here.

110
00:09:06,561 --> 00:09:10,611
He probably became a real warrior there.

111
00:09:12,901 --> 00:09:17,281
Thorfinn. How did he spend his time in Iceland?

112
00:09:17,361 --> 00:09:18,571
Tell me.

113
00:09:21,371 --> 00:09:22,661
I don't want to.

114
00:09:23,871 --> 00:09:26,041
I told you what I know!

115
00:09:26,121 --> 00:09:27,621
Shut up! I don't care.

116
00:09:27,711 --> 00:09:31,751
You cheapskate! It's not that you don't want to tell me.
You actually don't know.

117
00:09:32,251 --> 00:09:36,591
I can tell by looking in your eyes. You don't have
that same mysterious sparkle he does.

118
00:09:36,681 --> 00:09:37,511
What did you say?

119
00:09:37,591 --> 00:09:42,601
You didn't learn anything from Thors.
And you're embarrassed that I'd find out, right?

120
00:09:44,221 --> 00:09:45,561
Wait.

121
00:09:45,641 --> 00:09:47,601
Let go! I'll kill everyone starting with you!

122
00:09:47,691 --> 00:09:50,061
You'll lose if you fight like you usually do.

123
00:09:54,071 --> 00:09:55,191
See?

124
00:09:56,151 --> 00:09:59,661
Whether you win or lose will decide whether I live or die.

125
00:09:59,741 --> 00:10:01,201
That's why I'm going to tell you

126
00:10:02,531 --> 00:10:05,201
how to defeat that monster.

127
00:10:06,371 --> 00:10:07,871
Don't bullshit me, baldy!

128
00:10:08,251 --> 00:10:11,791
If you knew how to beat him, why didn't you fight him?

129
00:10:11,881 --> 00:10:15,131
Battle isn't the same as Shogi.

130
00:10:15,211 --> 00:10:17,971
It's not over just because you beat their captain.

131
00:10:19,131 --> 00:10:23,561
But this is different. He said if you win, he'll let us go.

132
00:10:23,641 --> 00:10:28,141
He values honor. He'll keep the vow he made
before the duel.

133
00:10:30,311 --> 00:10:32,771
Remember the reason you fight.

134
00:10:33,771 --> 00:10:35,981
It's to beat me in a duel, right?

135
00:10:38,951 --> 00:10:42,281
Let me be your advisor, just this once.

136
00:10:45,991 --> 00:10:50,251
So that the two of us can survive this situation.

137
00:11:00,341 --> 00:11:02,681
I wanted to see the captain's duel.

138
00:11:02,761 --> 00:11:06,061
If I die, I want to die in a duel with the captain, too.

139
00:11:06,141 --> 00:11:07,561
I'd be proud in Valhalla.

140
00:11:07,891 --> 00:11:11,731
He's on a different level. I bet he's a reincarnation
of Thors, the god of lightning.

141
00:11:11,811 --> 00:11:15,731
If the captain is Thors, then does that mean
Prince Canute is Freyja?

142
00:11:15,821 --> 00:11:17,281
She's a goddess!

143
00:11:21,661 --> 00:11:23,371
It's a reincarnation of Freyja!

144
00:11:25,121 --> 00:11:27,991
Take this!

145
00:11:30,581 --> 00:11:32,831
Does that hurt, Thorfinn?

146
00:11:32,921 --> 00:11:36,881
Why don't you just forget about Askeladd and surrender?

147
00:11:50,021 --> 00:11:51,311
You bastard!

148
00:11:51,391 --> 00:11:52,601
Don't run away!

149
00:11:52,691 --> 00:11:54,311
You don't know when to quit!

150
00:11:54,401 --> 00:11:58,821
Look at you! Fight to the end with pride!

151
00:11:58,901 --> 00:12:00,821
Are you trying to disgrace the name of Thors?

152
00:12:01,861 --> 00:12:03,701
Damn!

153
00:12:03,781 --> 00:12:05,821
Bear it for now, Thorfinn.

154
00:12:07,951 --> 00:12:10,621
Get him to come closer.

155
00:12:14,331 --> 00:12:16,961
Was it the Battle of Maldon?

156
00:12:19,001 --> 00:12:20,631
It was a fierce battle.

157
00:12:21,841 --> 00:12:25,091
Even Thorkell was severely wounded.

158
00:12:26,301 --> 00:12:27,471
It was only a moment.

159
00:12:28,601 --> 00:12:31,101
It was only a moment, but I saw it.

160
00:12:32,891 --> 00:12:36,401
I saw the moment that Thorkell the Invincible collapsed.

161
00:12:43,571 --> 00:12:48,581
That was good. Make him think that you've used up
everything you got.

162
00:12:48,661 --> 00:12:52,001
What's wrong, Thorfinn?
Are you tired of running away now?

163
00:12:56,461 --> 00:12:58,541
I'm so disappointed.

164
00:12:58,631 --> 00:13:01,671
I thought you had more spirit in you.

165
00:13:02,801 --> 00:13:05,881
You're in a good spot. Good job, Thorfinn.

166
00:13:05,971 --> 00:13:07,891
That was over fast.

167
00:13:07,971 --> 00:13:09,051
Pathetic.

168
00:13:09,141 --> 00:13:10,351
He ran away the whole time.

169
00:13:11,561 --> 00:13:13,931
That's right, Thorkell.

170
00:13:14,021 --> 00:13:15,891
Come finish him off.

171
00:13:18,231 --> 00:13:19,481
All that's left is...

172
00:13:20,981 --> 00:13:22,941
for you to let your guard down for a moment.

173
00:13:28,701 --> 00:13:30,201
His weakness is...

174
00:13:55,231 --> 00:13:56,771
Captain!

175
00:13:59,851 --> 00:14:02,231
You idiot! You don't have a weapon!

176
00:14:02,321 --> 00:14:03,531
Thorfinn! On your right!

177
00:14:06,861 --> 00:14:08,781
Kill that kid!

178
00:14:08,861 --> 00:14:10,031
Damn!

179
00:14:11,621 --> 00:14:13,291
Die, kid!

180
00:14:13,371 --> 00:14:17,081
Stop, you fools!

181
00:14:18,711 --> 00:14:23,671
You bastards... How dare you humiliate me!

182
00:14:23,751 --> 00:14:24,591
Captain!

183
00:14:24,671 --> 00:14:29,801
How dare you tarnish my duel!

184
00:14:35,221 --> 00:14:37,851
Asgeir, you...

185
00:14:37,931 --> 00:14:40,651
What about your honor as a warrior?

186
00:14:40,731 --> 00:14:43,611
I don't care if you hate me for it.
I'm going to kill that kid.

187
00:14:45,861 --> 00:14:48,491
If you want to kill me, then kill me!

188
00:14:48,571 --> 00:14:50,491
But you must live!

189
00:14:50,571 --> 00:14:51,781
No one else

190
00:14:51,871 --> 00:14:55,791
could unify these 500 beasts!

191
00:15:03,171 --> 00:15:04,541
Stop right there.

192
00:15:06,631 --> 00:15:08,591
You must not fight anymore.

193
00:15:13,091 --> 00:15:15,511
Whoever dies in this fight

194
00:15:15,601 --> 00:15:16,641
will die in vain.

195
00:15:19,521 --> 00:15:20,851
Impossible...

196
00:15:22,521 --> 00:15:27,731
They've been annihilated... Askeladd's army has been...

197
00:15:31,951 --> 00:15:32,781
Brother!

198
00:15:36,531 --> 00:15:37,791
You're alive!

199
00:15:41,541 --> 00:15:43,541
Who are you?

200
00:15:45,291 --> 00:15:46,631
Brother...

201
00:15:48,801 --> 00:15:53,431
How can you kill each other without end?
Don't you tire of it?

202
00:15:53,511 --> 00:15:57,561
I don't care if you're royalty.
You have no right to spoil the duel.

203
00:15:57,641 --> 00:15:59,811
Stay back, little girl.

204
00:16:01,851 --> 00:16:04,811
It doesn't look like a duel anymore.

205
00:16:04,901 --> 00:16:09,821
If you're a leader, you should show your men
pride and honor.

206
00:16:12,741 --> 00:16:18,281
Silence! I don't need you to tell me what I already know!

207
00:16:29,381 --> 00:16:32,971
Let Thorfinn go. I lost this duel.

208
00:16:33,051 --> 00:16:35,641
Captain! You haven't lost! We just got in the way!

209
00:16:35,721 --> 00:16:37,551
Shut up, you idiots!

210
00:16:39,261 --> 00:16:43,351
I lost. I should preserve my dignity.

211
00:16:43,441 --> 00:16:45,271
Asgeir...

212
00:16:45,351 --> 00:16:47,401
Do as the captain commands.

213
00:16:51,691 --> 00:16:54,031
That was unpleasant.

214
00:16:54,111 --> 00:16:58,121
I've been alive for 50 years, but I've never
had a day as bad as today.

215
00:17:00,241 --> 00:17:01,491
Booze!

216
00:17:03,001 --> 00:17:05,371
Hey, baldy! Let's get away right now!

217
00:17:05,461 --> 00:17:07,711
If you want to go, then go. I'm staying.

218
00:17:07,791 --> 00:17:10,671
What? What do you think I went through all that for?

219
00:17:10,751 --> 00:17:12,131
Just shut up and watch.

220
00:17:16,431 --> 00:17:21,971
So? Who do you think you are, prince?
Did you just stroll over to break up the fight?

221
00:17:22,061 --> 00:17:24,641
I wish to have your sled and your supplies.

222
00:17:24,731 --> 00:17:28,021
And Thorfinn and Askeladd are my followers.

223
00:17:28,101 --> 00:17:30,061
I'm taking them.

224
00:17:30,151 --> 00:17:32,111
Are you stupid?

225
00:17:32,191 --> 00:17:34,991
What kind of a hunter would let his prey get away?

226
00:17:38,361 --> 00:17:41,201
You intend to use me to bargain
with King Sweyn.

227
00:17:42,911 --> 00:17:45,291
Is that what you're thinking?

228
00:17:45,371 --> 00:17:47,501
Yes, prince.

229
00:17:47,581 --> 00:17:50,921
You're bait. You're a hostage.
And you're a source of money.

230
00:17:51,001 --> 00:17:53,711
Forget about the prince! Don't get greedy!

231
00:17:53,801 --> 00:17:55,171
Just watch!

232
00:17:56,971 --> 00:17:59,431
Stay back, lout. I won't run away.

233
00:18:03,351 --> 00:18:07,811
You matured a lot in a short amount of time.
What happened?

234
00:18:09,061 --> 00:18:12,231
I found Ragnar's corpse in the village
I stopped by yesterday.

235
00:18:16,861 --> 00:18:17,821
Thorkell.

236
00:18:18,911 --> 00:18:20,821
I have no value as a hostage.

237
00:18:21,951 --> 00:18:23,411
The reason being...

238
00:18:25,081 --> 00:18:26,791
my father

239
00:18:26,871 --> 00:18:29,331
doesn't love me.

240
00:18:31,171 --> 00:18:35,051
My father is going to give the throne
to my brother Harald.

241
00:18:35,131 --> 00:18:37,671
I'm just second to my brother.

242
00:18:39,381 --> 00:18:43,301
However, that caused the vassals to start fighting,

243
00:18:43,391 --> 00:18:45,851
and endangered the foundation of the kingdom.

244
00:18:48,181 --> 00:18:50,521
My existence

245
00:18:50,601 --> 00:18:52,941
is a source of distress to the king.

246
00:18:54,481 --> 00:19:00,361
In other words, King Sweyn is hoping that I'll kill you?

247
00:19:00,451 --> 00:19:03,951
It'd be better to have me die in battle
than to assassinate me.

248
00:19:04,031 --> 00:19:06,831
It would allow my father to avoid killing his own child.

249
00:19:07,751 --> 00:19:11,421
If I did let you go right now, where would you go?

250
00:19:12,541 --> 00:19:15,131
To the main camp in Gainsborough.

251
00:19:16,461 --> 00:19:19,301
To fight my father, the king.

252
00:19:22,681 --> 00:19:25,891
You think you can win? Congratulations.

253
00:19:25,971 --> 00:19:27,851
I'm doing what should be done.

254
00:19:28,851 --> 00:19:32,191
My life isn't valuable anyway.

255
00:19:42,491 --> 00:19:47,831
I've seen lots of men who said
they didn't care about their life.

256
00:19:48,951 --> 00:19:53,211
But most of them cry and beg for their life as soon as
they get hit, even if it's just a light punch.

257
00:19:55,291 --> 00:19:58,211
You're just like them, right?

258
00:20:12,521 --> 00:20:16,441
I hate that look in his eyes. I've seen it before.

259
00:20:21,491 --> 00:20:24,911
What are you looking at with those eyes?

260
00:20:27,411 --> 00:20:29,661
What happened? They got quiet.

261
00:20:32,461 --> 00:20:33,541
Men.

262
00:20:34,541 --> 00:20:38,801
Even I have one thing I regret.

263
00:20:40,551 --> 00:20:44,801
I regret not following Thors back there.

264
00:20:46,591 --> 00:20:49,141
If I had followed him then,

265
00:20:49,221 --> 00:20:52,271
I would have learned
the secret to being a real warrior.

266
00:20:56,771 --> 00:21:00,111
Well, I'm going to end up fighting King Sweyn anyway.

267
00:21:02,191 --> 00:21:03,611
All right! I've made my decision.

268
00:21:06,031 --> 00:21:08,451
I'll help you fight.

269
00:21:10,581 --> 00:21:12,581
I'm going to follow you.

270
00:21:13,621 --> 00:21:17,961
I'm going to watch what you do from now on,
and who you'll become.

271
00:21:19,131 --> 00:21:22,211
But if you do anything soft, I'm going to kill you.

272
00:21:24,551 --> 00:21:28,591
Good. From today on, you, too, are one of my followers.

273
00:21:29,971 --> 00:21:31,681
Then what about us?

274
00:21:31,761 --> 00:21:34,481
Well, the captain says he's going to follow him, so...

275
00:21:41,441 --> 00:21:44,191
What's wrong with him?
What's he still doing here?

276
00:21:59,751 --> 00:22:01,131
Your Highness Canute.

277
00:22:03,501 --> 00:22:06,761
I'm the one who killed Ragnar.

278
00:22:06,841 --> 00:22:08,131
Please kill me.

279
00:22:10,761 --> 00:22:12,601
However,

280
00:22:12,681 --> 00:22:15,431
if you let me live,

281
00:22:15,521 --> 00:22:17,061
I shall help you,

282
00:22:18,191 --> 00:22:20,271
even if it costs me my life.

283
00:22:25,691 --> 00:22:29,911
Work on his behalf, too.
That's how you shall mourn his death.

284
00:22:31,121 --> 00:22:32,161
Certainly.

285
00:22:38,161 --> 00:22:40,171
If you want to come with me, then come.

286
00:22:41,501 --> 00:22:44,961
We're going to drag King Sweyn down from the throne.

287
00:22:46,461 --> 00:22:49,131
What are you doing? Don't copy me.

288
00:22:49,221 --> 00:22:53,931
I'm not. I'm the one who became his vassal first.

289
00:22:54,011 --> 00:22:56,971
Anyway, let's be friends.

290
00:22:57,061 --> 00:23:01,101
I killed most of your men,
but it's water under the bridge, right?

291
00:23:04,731 --> 00:23:09,031
Letting it be water under the bridge
is the only thing you can do.
